From 6508a47cf1431a18b42d80167cdb0b02376f6313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Quota episode: another gateway's wall holds only
 while this pool agrees

A hinted quota_episode takes its deadline from the recording worker's own
OAuth pool, but decision() held the card on every gateway until that
deadline. On 2026-11-12 nine cards sat on subscription_quota_reset for 1-6
days on Anthropic walls recorded by worker-6/worker-2 while worker-5's pool
had three accounts with Opus room (t_01a1cf8d39b99b11).

decision() now drops a wall when this gateway did not just see it itself
(the walled run's claim lock is another host's, or our own wall is older
than LOCAL_WALL_TRUST_SECONDS = 30 min) and this pool has positive room for
every walled provider on the concrete model (a class wall checks the
class's routes for that provider). Room needs a live OAuth entry with no
quota/bench cooldown (new quota_room / live_quota_room), so an empty, dead
or unreadable pool never lifts a wall. A wall this gateway just saw, and a
wall with no recorded provider, hold as before. If the run hits the wall
here, its new episode holds it on this gateway.
